-- coa29-tests-sch7.l4: tests for coa29-sch7.l4 (Schedule 7: parent and subsidiary undertakings: supplementary provisions).
-- Generated by work/gen_tests_sch7.py. Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Schedule, beside the case; none is
-- copied from the encoding's output. Quote lines live in the module, not here.


§§ `Para 2: voting rights in an undertaking`

-- Para 2(1): the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares (or, for an undertaking with no share capital, on members) to vote at general meetings on all, or substantially all, matters.
-- a share capital; shareholders' rights in respect of shares; general meetings; all or substantially all matters
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has a share capital` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on members` IS FALSE, `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS TRUE, `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- as above but only on some matters
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has a share capital` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on members` IS FALSE, `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS TRUE, `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- as above but not to vote at general meetings
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has a share capital` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on members` IS FALSE, `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS FALSE, `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a share capital: rights conferred on members who are not shareholders in respect of their shares
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has a share capital` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS FALSE, `the rights are conferred on members` IS TRUE, `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS TRUE, `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no share capital: rights conferred on members
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has a share capital` IS FALSE, `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS FALSE, `the rights are conferred on members` IS TRUE, `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS TRUE, `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no share capital: rights conferred on shareholders in respect of shares
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has a share capital` IS FALSE, `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS TRUE, `the rights are conferred on members` IS FALSE, `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS TRUE, `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Para 2(2): where the undertaking has no general meetings deciding matters by votes, holding a majority of the voting rights means having the right under its constitution to direct its overall policy or to alter the terms of its constitution.
-- no general meetings; the right to direct the overall policy
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(2) the undertaking holds a majority of the voting rights in the other undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS FALSE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to direct its overall policy` IS TRUE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to alter the terms of its constitution` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no general meetings; the right to alter the terms of the constitution
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(2) the undertaking holds a majority of the voting rights in the other undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS FALSE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to direct its overall policy` IS FALSE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to alter the terms of its constitution` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no general meetings; neither right
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(2) the undertaking holds a majority of the voting rights in the other undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS FALSE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to direct its overall policy` IS FALSE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to alter the terms of its constitution` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the undertaking has general meetings deciding matters by votes: paragraph 2(2) is not about it
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 2(2) the undertaking holds a majority of the voting rights in the other undertaking` WITH `the undertaking has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS TRUE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to direct its overall policy` IS TRUE, `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to alter the terms of its constitution` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Para 3: the right to appoint or remove a majority of the directors`

-- Para 3(1): directors holding a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the board on all, or substantially all, matters. A majority is more than half.
-- 3 of 4 votes
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` WITH `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS 3, `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS 4, `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 of 4 votes: exactly half is not a majority
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` WITH `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS 2, `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS 4, `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 of 1 vote
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` WITH `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS 1, `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS 1, `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 of 5 votes
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` WITH `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS 2, `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS 5, `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 3 of 4 votes, but not on all or substantially all matters
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` WITH `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS 3, `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS 4, `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no votes at meetings of the board at all
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` WITH `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS 0, `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS 0, `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 3(2)(a)
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) the undertaking is treated as having the right to appoint to the directorship` WITH `a person's appointment to the directorship follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the undertaking` IS TRUE, `the directorship is held by the undertaking itself` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 3(2)(b)
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) the undertaking is treated as having the right to appoint to the directorship` WITH `a person's appointment to the directorship follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the undertaking` IS FALSE, `the directorship is held by the undertaking itself` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither limb (an unmet 'if': marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) the undertaking is treated as having the right to appoint to the directorship` WITH `a person's appointment to the directorship follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the undertaking` IS FALSE, `the directorship is held by the undertaking itself` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 3(3): not a consent-only right
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(3) the right is taken into account` WITH `the right is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person` IS FALSE, `no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- para 3(3): consent-only and no other person has a right
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(3) the right is taken into account` WITH `the right is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person` IS TRUE, `no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 3(3): consent-only and another person has a right
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(3) the right is taken into account` WITH `the right is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person` IS TRUE, `no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Para 4: the right to exercise a dominant influence`

-- Para 4(1): not regarded as having a dominant influence unless it has a right to give directions on operating and financial policies that the directors are obliged to comply with whether or not they benefit the other undertaking. The function answers the bar: JUST TRUE where it applies, JUST FALSE where the 'unless' is met (the text does not say the undertaking IS then regarded as having the right).
-- a right to give directions that the directors must comply with whether or not for the benefit of the other undertaking: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(1) the undertaking cannot be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence` WITH `the undertaking has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of the other undertaking` IS TRUE, `the directors of the other undertaking are obliged to comply with the directions whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a right to give directions, but the directors are not so obliged: the bar applies
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(1) the undertaking cannot be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence` WITH `the undertaking has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of the other undertaking` IS TRUE, `the directors of the other undertaking are obliged to comply with the directions whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- directors obliged but no right to give directions: the bar applies
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(1) the undertaking cannot be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence` WITH `the undertaking has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of the other undertaking` IS FALSE, `the directors of the other undertaking are obliged to comply with the directions whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither: the bar applies
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(1) the undertaking cannot be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence` WITH `the undertaking has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of the other undertaking` IS FALSE, `the directors of the other undertaking are obliged to comply with the directions whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Para 4(2): a control contract is a contract in writing conferring such a right which (a) is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking and (b) is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established.
-- all four elements
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(2) the contract is a control contract` WITH `the contract is in writing` IS TRUE, `the contract confers such a right` IS TRUE, `the contract is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable` IS TRUE, `the contract is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a contract that is not in writing
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(2) the contract is a control contract` WITH `the contract is in writing` IS FALSE, `the contract confers such a right` IS TRUE, `the contract is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable` IS TRUE, `the contract is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contract that is does not confer such a right
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(2) the contract is a control contract` WITH `the contract is in writing` IS TRUE, `the contract confers such a right` IS FALSE, `the contract is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable` IS TRUE, `the contract is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contract that is not of a kind authorised by the articles
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(2) the contract is a control contract` WITH `the contract is in writing` IS TRUE, `the contract confers such a right` IS TRUE, `the contract is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable` IS FALSE, `the contract is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contract that is not permitted by the law of establishment
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(2) the contract is a control contract` WITH `the contract is in writing` IS TRUE, `the contract confers such a right` IS TRUE, `the contract is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable` IS TRUE, `the contract is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 4(3): for section 1162(4)(a): paragraph 4 is not to be read as affecting it (a flat negative)
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(3) paragraph 4 affects the construction of section 1162(4)(a)` WITH `the provision in question is section 1162(4)(a)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 4(3): another provision: not decided
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 4(3) paragraph 4 affects the construction of section 1162(4)(a)` WITH `the provision in question is section 1162(4)(a)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paras 5 to 7: circumstances; fiduciary; nominee`

-- Para 5(1): rights exercisable only in certain circumstances are taken into account only (a) when the circumstances have arisen and for so long as they continue, or (b) when within the control of the person having them. Para 5(2): normally exercisable but temporarily incapable: taken into account.
-- conditional; the circumstances have arisen and continue
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 5 the rights are taken into account` WITH `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS TRUE, `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS TRUE, `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS FALSE, `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- conditional; within the control of the holder
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 5 the rights are taken into account` WITH `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS TRUE, `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS FALSE, `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS TRUE, `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- conditional; neither
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 5 the rights are taken into account` WITH `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS TRUE, `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS FALSE, `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS FALSE, `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- normally exercisable but temporarily incapable
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 5 the rights are taken into account` WITH `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS FALSE, `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS FALSE, `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS FALSE, `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ordinary rights: silent
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 5 the rights are taken into account` WITH `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS FALSE, `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS FALSE, `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS FALSE, `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- conditional, neither limb, and temporarily incapable: sub-paragraph (1) governs
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 5 the rights are taken into account` WITH `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS TRUE, `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS FALSE, `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS FALSE, `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 6: held in a fiduciary capacity
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 6 the rights are treated as not held by the person who holds them` WITH `the rights are held in a fiduciary capacity` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 6: not held in a fiduciary capacity
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 6 the rights are treated as not held by the person who holds them` WITH `the rights are held in a fiduciary capacity` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- para 7(2): exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 7(2) the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another` WITH `the rights are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 7(2): not so exercisable (an unmet 'if': marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 7(2) the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another` WITH `the rights are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 7(1): held by a person as nominee for another
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 7(1) the rights are treated as held by the other` WITH `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another` IS TRUE, `the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another under paragraph 7(2)` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 7(1): regarded as held as nominee under para 7(2)
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 7(1) the rights are treated as held by the other` WITH `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another` IS FALSE, `the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another under paragraph 7(2)` IS JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 7(1): neither
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 7(1) the rights are treated as held by the other` WITH `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another` IS FALSE, `the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another under paragraph 7(2)` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- para 7(1): not a nominee; para 7(2) not decided
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 7(1) the rights are treated as held by the other` WITH `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another` IS FALSE, `the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another under paragraph 7(2)` IS NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

